{"id": "129801", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=129801", "title": "Altenkirchen (Mecklenburg-Vorpommern)", "text": "Altenkirchen is a small town and district on the island of R\u00fcgen.\nUnderstand.\nAltenkirchen is a historic municipality with around 1,000 inhabitants on the Wittow Peninsula, at the northern tip of R\u00fcgen. It serves as a central hub for several smaller settlements, including Drewoldke, Gudderitz, Lanckensburg, Mattchow, Schwarbe, Presenske, Wollin, and Z\u00fchlitz.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nOn the L30 just north of Breege-Juliusruh\nBuy.\nThe village is a practical stop for supplies. Along the main road L30, you will find a Netto supermarket, a beverage store, a Sparkasse bank, and a small department store for clothing and household goods."}
{"id": "129806", "revid": "2282211", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=129806", "title": "Schaprode", "text": "Schaprode is a village on the island of R\u00fcgen.\nUnderstand.\nThe small harbour is one of the access points to the island of Hiddensee with a and water taxis.\nAs no cars are allowed on Hiddensee many people drive to Schaprode then go by foot or bike from here. The village has basically become a large car park.\nGet in.\nThe village is 24 km from Bergen auf R\u00fcgen by country roads. Alternatively by boat from Hiddensee.\nSleep.\nThere are a number of holiday apartments to rent as well as a camp-site."}
{"id": "129823", "revid": "2432955", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=129823", "title": "Leribe", "text": "Leribe is in the north of Lesotho. Established in the 19th century by a British missionary, this town on the banks of the Hlotse river was one of the main centres in colonial days. Today, it's home to some 25,000 people and is a good place for travellers to find whatever last supplies they need to head out into Lesotho's gorgeous highlands. It has two major towns Hlotse, a market town, and Maputsoe the industrial hub.\nGet in.\nBuses/minibuses are available from the Maseru transit station for around 35 maloti or rand (Apr 2014). Takes around 1.5-4 hours, depending on route (may detour to Maputsoe before heading to Leribe). From the North, frequent minibuses can be found plying the route between Butha-Buthe and Hlotse for around 30 maloti or rand (Apr 2014). The road is in fairly good condition between Maseru and Butha-Buthe.\nGet around.\nHlotse/Leribe is a fairly small town, and relatively easy to get around by foot. There are some taxis and minibuses available.\nSee.\nThe oldest building in the city is the 1877 Anglican Church. Near the market place, you'll see the Gun Tower, a relic of the 1866 Gun War. Also notice the old English statue, another relic from colonial days, in the centre of town.\nBuy.\nWhen entering the city you'll see the Leribe Craft Center along the road, which is a nice place for souvenirs. For sale are many different mohair products, made by physically disabled and deaf women from the region. You'll find anything from dolls and handbags to clothing, all in local designs. The centre is a long-running project of the Anglican church.\nEat.\nThere are several small restaurants and bars to choose from. Alternatively, many Chinese 'supermarkets' and a Shoprite are also available for groceries."}
