{"id": "129950", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=129950", "title": "Topanga", "text": "Topanga is an unincorporated community of Los Angeles County, surrounded by the Santa Monica Mountains National Recreation Area. Topanga has long been a getaway for artists and musicians, and it retains a distinct bohemian flavor, which is complemented by the outdoor enthusiasts who have escaped the urban tangle to be closer to nature. In 2020, it was home to about 8,600 people.\nGet in.\nTopanga can be reached most directly by taking Topanga Canyon Boulevard north from Pacific Coast Highway in Malibu, or south Route 101 from the San Fernando Valley. Old Topanga Canyon Road and La Tuna Canyon Road are also available, but are older and more indirect routes."}
{"id": "129957", "revid": "144844", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=129957", "title": "Niepo\u0142omice", "text": "Niepo\u0142omice is a town in Ma\u0142opolskie Province in the south of Poland, 25 km southeast of Krak\u00f3w. Its big attraction is the Royal Castle. \nGet in.\nMany private buses and also public communication from Krak\u00f3w. Public bus lines 211, 221 and 301 from Krak\u00f3w go to Niepo\u0142omice. It is best to get off at the stops \"Niepo\u0142omice Rynek\" or \"Niepo\u0142omice Dworzec\".\nGet around.\nNiepo\u0142omice is small enough to cover all of it on foot."}
